entDynamic1I1" decimals="-5" unitRef="INR">1077700000</in-capmkt:OriginalAllocation><in-capmkt:ModifiedAllocation contextRef="StatementDynamic1I1" decimals="-5" unitRef="INR">43400000</in-capmkt:ModifiedAllocation><in-capmkt:FundsUtilised contextRef="StatementDynamic1I1" decimals="-5" unitRef="INR">43400000</in-capmkt:FundsUtilised><in-capmkt:AmountOfDeviationOrVariationForTheQuarterAccordingToApplicableObject contextRef="StatementDynamic1I1" decimals="-5" unitRef="INR">0</in-capmkt:AmountOfDeviationOrVariationForTheQuarterAccordingToApplicableObject><in-capmkt:DisclosureNotesOnObjectsForWhichFundsHaveBeenRaisedAndWhereThereHasBeenADeviation contextRef="StatementDynamic1I1">•  In the preferential issue, Adventz Finance Private Limited and Samena Green Limited subscribed to 38,86,010 warrants each at an issue price of Rs.193 per warrant, with the Company initially receiving 25% of the issue price (Rs.3,750 lakhs). On 9 October 2025, at the time of payment of remaining subscription amount Adventz Finance paid full amount in respect of all  warrants subscribed by it and was allotted 38,86,010 equity shares. Samena Green paid remaining subscription amount in respect of 35,11,260 warrants only and was allotted an equivalent number of equity shares. Due to short payment of final subscription amount, the remaining 3,74,750 warrants of Samena Green lapsed on 12 October 2025 and amount paid initially at the time of allotment was forfeited . As a result of short receipt of funds, the amount earmarked for Capital Expenditure got reduced from Rs.11,500 lakhs to Rs.10,777 lakhs.  &lt;br /&gt; 
 &lt;br /&gt; 
•  Due to geopolitical uncertainties, the Company could utilise only Rs.434 lakhs towards Capital Expenditure and got the shareholders approval for the change in utilisation of the remaining Rs.10,343 lakhs from Capital Expenditure to Working Capital Requirements through Postal Ballot Resolution dated 13 April 2026.  &lt;br /&gt; 
• The revised objects Capital Expenditure (Rs.434 lakhs), Working Capital Requirements (Rs.10,343 lakhs) and General Corporate Purposes (Rs.3,500 lakhs) have been fully utilised for the relevant objects within 30th June 2026. &lt;br /&gt; 
